I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378247} {:answer/id #uuid "94d62c48-c41c-5fbc-9d7a-f4d1a6557b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378248} {:answer/id #uuid "56d6d423-5656-501e-b2f6-2c600eecf510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fddf6f5d-eb46-55d9-bafa-dfcde8802b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378246} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0ce217c-40ee-5b1e-ac1e-80701505ad04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "097f179d-8b94-55d4-8f36-ac53f5125474" :question/math-academy-id "q-104930" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are finite?\n\n- $P(N)$\n- $P({Z,\\pi })$\n- $P({x\\in Z∣\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0})$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of a finite set is finite, while the power set of an infinite set is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Set I is infinite since the underlying set $N$ is infinite.\n\n- Set II is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\nP({Z,\\pi })={∅,\\,{Z},\\,{\\pi },\\,{Z,\\pi }}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $4.$\n\n- Set III is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\n{x\\in Z∣\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0}={0},\n$$\n\nand, as a result, \n\n$$\nP({x\\in Z∣\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0})=P({0})={∅,\\,{0}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060113 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "871a7617-5883-54c8-9745-ccda8b526b38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057037} {:answer/id #uuid "c38869d4-7e70-54e4-aa9a-df7864f2559a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057038} {:answer/id #uuid "da12571e-3a0a-5c9e-82f3-a71442fefc49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057039} {:answer/id #uuid "06b20c6d-4149-51cd-89bd-f13d224528b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057040} {:answer/id #uuid "7a6d0636-7799-50e9-8446-ae1ecf71fea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057041}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4c5ba7e8-f49b-5ea6-8c98-ac67aae3ec8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057036} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b811f16-43eb-5f85-84c8-55929421d66f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378983} {:answer/id #uuid "78a24d3f-be42-5f68-a888-0034cc2ef78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378984} {:answer/id #uuid "0118e984-414e-5948-aa4c-f8da0babefc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378985} {:answer/id #uuid "69d0ce7a-a4de-5d93-b271-a087f1d61b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378986} {:answer/id #uuid "547d50fe-8135-5c3f-9493-d83c061ec333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "547d50fe-8135-5c3f-9493-d83c061ec333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378987} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b0553c1-dc69-5b86-83b2-1778e74ee087" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37ad276a-88ce-596c-9a24-406a32aa6e25" :question/math-academy-id "q-171334" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** $10\\ge 1,$ **then** $3\\in R.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\n- If $10<1,$ then $3\\notin R.$\n- If $3\\notin R,$ then $10<1.$\n- If $3\\in R,$ then $10\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/d9/d946d2a81d46cbde934ebbab54f9b69b514092e02da4f8a3b79768f218929449.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement I is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement II is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement III is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064612 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064163 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e901ea71-aeab-5e95-939e-2401558aa708" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Global Extrema of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90e11493-093d-5677-9cce-796074ba130e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061750} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d8e750-c89b-5ba7-b458-68ac026f484a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061751} {:answer/id #uuid "d85f6949-16e9-59c0-8f4b-cd4eba8557d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061752} {:answer/id #uuid "1d8ae605-3c4c-5bbe-bc7a-ba41af30bda2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061753} {:answer/id #uuid "7aec39cd-06b6-51e7-8fac-330d7d637bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061754}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9c6adffb-ec69-5386-895c-90f005cfeb37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061749} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae1b3034-251a-59f4-b113-773134be1def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396649} {:answer/id #uuid "b0a7e325-bb6e-50d6-8115-8a687cfd729f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396650} {:answer/id #uuid "b53f607f-c200-5ff6-8ced-e452dc4d4a4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396651} {:answer/id #uuid "dc8d5f4e-4f95-5ba3-ba2b-62b542d4c351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396652} {:answer/id #uuid "0481ca8b-da90-5343-99ae-63643fac6ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0a7e325-bb6e-50d6-8115-8a687cfd729f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396650} :answer-field/id #uuid "041ff950-f3f8-5661-8897-41d87f43abe3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396648}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "542cb4a0-6380-5eaf-91e8-44f9300f10c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-22428" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ defined on the closed interval $\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le e,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The global maximum value is $\\frac{1}{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$\nII. The global minimum value is $e-2$\nIII. The global minimum value is $2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=1-\\frac{2}{x},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n1-\\frac{2}{x}=0\\,⟹\\,x=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=2,$ and the endpoints $x=\\frac{1}{2},e$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2≈1.9 \\\\ f(2) & =2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2≈0.6 \\\\ f(e) & =e-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e=e-2≈0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,$ so the global maximum is $\\frac{1}{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(2)=2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,$ so the global minimum is $2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"I and III only.\"\n\n![](images/6c/6cc3ee476c8c5dc9e27051c990b184318147caffd2177b760074172fe5c667f6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "865035a9-dfe6-51bf-a5dc-624240267541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087156} {:answer/id #uuid "981d3229-34da-5547-9622-76e7a57b9b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087157} {:answer/id #uuid "ff08f834-c93c-58b6-a6eb-be4ab302b1ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087158} {:answer/id #uuid "5826ab39-99cb-5f0d-a91a-c8e47d4e7431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087159} {:answer/id #uuid "58fc334c-401e-58ca-8084-7bbee1c81411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087160}] :answer-field/id #uuid "212166f2-0485-5ec6-aaa6-538998150651" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087155} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9010786-eb95-569b-8bf6-50b7c4d11251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396198} {:answer/id #uuid "9017ed40-b00d-55a3-877f-c3d4b075da7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396199} {:answer/id #uuid "e2a1da3a-abde-5c78-94f6-9beb1ca8472a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396200} {:answer/id #uuid "8a2fc306-e79b-5a44-8145-c511e597d027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396201} {:answer/id #uuid "8b5eb027-48d1-5f9c-9af9-618b997023bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9010786-eb95-569b-8bf6-50b7c4d11251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396198} :answer-field/id #uuid "169533db-26aa-5a83-a7a7-fa42593fd137" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9a96319-3bb3-5dd4-a3ac-27f5effab07d" :question/math-academy-id "q-8331" :question/problem "Let \n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\nII. $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\nIII. $T$ is a linear transformation" :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}]=kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}], \\\\  & T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}ky \\\\ kx\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =k[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "817ec199-0565-53e4-8206-076c4cf7c0a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099616} {:answer/id #uuid "870da87b-4483-59f0-b257-80a06f5553e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099617} {:answer/id #uuid "f11b07fd-5ac1-58a6-8b10-debb052aab82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099618} {:answer/id #uuid "2935fa50-cb13-5572-bb18-a0e7989736c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099619} {:answer/id #uuid "2b5da84e-3db1-5a16-bde9-d9f42c48baeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099620}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e51f60e0-c55d-5e98-8bd0-9bcaa73bb7ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099615} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a355126-1182-5b56-87b6-9e46cb5cc71a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402811} {:answer/id #uuid "bff037e1-78fd-597d-a2cc-cfcaa9132c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402812} {:answer/id #uuid "4f7fabcd-36ae-58b0-87d4-d8ecadab32be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402813} {:answer/id #uuid "21da0e63-7d44-5e1d-a482-ba5640f5bd5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402814} {:answer/id #uuid "4ef29f12-1148-5d1b-91ab-01ba28b7b9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a355126-1182-5b56-87b6-9e46cb5cc71a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402811} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bbaa81d-9156-5f56-9880-e18958600dcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59f14d04-9b7d-5b14-8363-a42027c3b11c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42374" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -0 & 6\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statement are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\nI. The product $AB$ is well defined\nII. The product $BA$ is well defined\nIII. The product $AC$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that all three statements are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105861 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16a6f0f7-4003-5908-8b1b-68d218fdcb8f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98eaa221-8061-5360-9f3a-01aff790f77b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102199} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0b4123-0689-5cc0-91e4-fe68191829a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102200} {:answer/id #uuid "222c2963-14d0-507d-a97e-ffcc989fb305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102201} {:answer/id #uuid "619c0be8-ca29-5bf3-8965-bbbd3aeb8b10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102202} {:answer/id #uuid "667230f0-b5dc-5751-9cd6-f1e948e6ced5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102203}] :answer-field/id #uuid "68775be3-9272-5bc9-9100-005d6326d43a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102198} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef8ace35-9c95-576a-890f-6128f5112c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369840} {:answer/id #uuid "b89d07a7-e31e-5fe2-91ec-380ad9991e78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369841} {:answer/id #uuid "9809aaf2-c6df-537f-994f-dca7d70205db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369842} {:answer/id #uuid "376f777d-e5fc-5e11-acc6-583c6da18efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369843} {:answer/id #uuid "46c6197f-377e-5c2f-b8de-89b584663a84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46c6197f-377e-5c2f-b8de-89b584663a84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369844} :answer-field/id #uuid "682fac89-b004-5da3-9d08-d368a37fd44e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ed6c6ac-3d65-5bdf-b16d-eef1fafdf163" :question/math-academy-id "q-154690" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f299f0d25bfee9303a6485413d44f1a6ce7b863c79ccae91f4f8d5d604f2bac3.png)\n\nConsider the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{4},\\, & 0\\le x<4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in [0,4)$\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. $f(x)$ is negative for some values of $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{x-1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x-1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-x]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\frac{16}{2}-4]-[\\frac{0}{2}-0]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(8-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement I is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d25a77b-7977-50b2-b375-51b8539bc9b9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Type of a Polygon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d73652a6-e0fb-5edd-8b1d-4c8e33523046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103168} {:answer/id #uuid "ffe398b2-a386-5f7a-baac-a95a30763e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103169} {:answer/id #uuid "025893e2-ba14-55e6-91d8-629ece66e2fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103170} {:answer/id #uuid "4c16cdda-9602-5b26-a3ac-71c143b32261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103171} {:answer/id #uuid "64aa948d-aae3-5c5e-aec2-be07dee5c91e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffe398b2-a386-5f7a-baac-a95a30763e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103169} :answer-field/id #uuid "0740a1b6-042c-517d-8516-9d8104534e5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18613fbc-efad-5e39-8673-d89aa94c710c" :question/math-academy-id "q-236888" :question/problem "![](images/10/102620aa55d15a8c07dc8224fd4de06d91cbd2abbbde6ee812df85a4862dc566.png)\n\nWhich of the above polygons are complex?" :question/worked-solution "A polygon is **simple** if its boundary does not intersect itself. Otherwise, the polygon is called **complex**.\n\nAmong the given polygons, only polygon II has intersecting sides. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32467c2c-5605-50e9-b961-a29535a0effb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99957751-2587-5b25-9134-94c034beb446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103931} {:answer/id #uuid "e0932cda-7dde-5be8-880f-c9fb2a213d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103932} {:answer/id #uuid "1143dbe1-d900-54f9-8c9e-6f7ce19bea71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103933} {:answer/id #uuid "3762eb77-1230-5403-b2fb-b8c47fa02c1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103934} {:answer/id #uuid "6d0f21ab-bdff-509e-82f7-50e3e4ab1f93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103935}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5319d510-514c-5b48-b87b-6ed0d2fbb222" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103930} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd129ace-39ab-53fd-a35a-3123900561ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370861} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4de8bb-6e16-5ab7-8991-e6d597a6f8bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370862} {:answer/id #uuid "ee9cec83-4385-583c-a89c-4555fba3af7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370863} {:answer/id #uuid "2c71fcad-cfa7-5a0b-b267-6f77c29ecb10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370864} {:answer/id #uuid "b2c6d885-533e-5717-9a05-16c9518eb9ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2c6d885-533e-5717-9a05-16c9518eb9ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370865} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e57de48-558b-52c6-bdda-b1f60df5f00f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b717856-6a11-5857-bbda-def4fc991b4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-36792" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $v=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2.$\n- $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =0.$\n- If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2,$ then $3v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda =6.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ With that in mind, let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $Av=v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =1$ (but not $2$).\n\n- Statement II is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{v}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $Av=0v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(3v)=3Av=3(2v)=2(3v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince, $A(3v)=2(3v),$ and $3v\\ne 0,$ this implies that $3v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =2$ (but not $6$).\n\n**Note:** In general, any non-zero multiple of an eigenvector is again an eigenvector, and the corresponding eigenvalue is the same.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110674 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f67c3319-1153-51ed-a57a-f85c06c7e76c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Points on Intersecting Lines Are Collinear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab463a2d-5905-58f7-af68-2bb4b2f11fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107322} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5b688b-0323-5661-8259-9b195cde3e07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107323} {:answer/id #uuid "e27df00f-7404-5963-a875-5f57e801702e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107324} {:answer/id #uuid "eb426f3b-b1df-57a8-8520-bb401013cc4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107325} {:answer/id #uuid "40830f1d-0ff2-52bd-bc13-247a6b6c50f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e27df00f-7404-5963-a875-5f57e801702e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107324} :answer-field/id #uuid "d078c165-bd3b-5097-be93-c04451228952" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5df118a-6629-591e-bac9-243a7536e271" :question/math-academy-id "q-13445" :question/problem "![](images/36/36ea34524b2ca277e8061441492711d36c8065e765d519d85d4008da97c3f8b3.png)\n\nConsider the figure shown above. Which of the following triplets of points are collinear?\n\nI. $M,N,R$\n\nII. $P,S,T$\n\nIII. $O,P,S$" :question/worked-solution "- $M,N,R$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/b8/b8fae613772422b14fce2e2db0762f659599f0b17409223ec291802b5d760d9c.png)\n\n- $P,S,T$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/85/85638c1466360f3e5285c34e84903824140b9e2fc72a0f029ab1ded170b64eb2.png)\n\n- $O,P,S$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/4b/4b7ef30e306e3c7e70dadb1524e1f60a9ea01832215009ef2ea8344cb07e7297.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9ef4e321-841e-5933-b5e4-ff7dab6c5275" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Collinear Points on a Grid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ec68db2-863b-55ad-8b69-eefdfc5401ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107466} {:answer/id #uuid "af56ea0b-013c-519d-a19e-24c5eecb6eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107467} {:answer/id #uuid "269504ce-2a6a-5ccd-9cf4-5b401742671b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107468} {:answer/id #uuid "5b210728-6a80-5b8f-97a2-05caf904c89a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107469} {:answer/id #uuid "7ddee60b-d64d-5874-a34e-03b6baff8ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "269504ce-2a6a-5ccd-9cf4-5b401742671b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107468} :answer-field/id #uuid "e907c4ba-8343-5fdd-abfe-8b39f70e8112" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ea9e0d7-7c8f-5224-8f6f-e5c31c36ab4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-155503" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bb96a7692787ca6e055b41d4f1599b87baa1ea331544ea42235a7131343c76e3.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams above shows three collinear points?" :question/worked-solution "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Diagram I shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/54/54735541d4dfc424fe186ddabe0c3f9d3cbd45a0dc7a1b8f4551cf8c5e5bc14f.png)\n\n- Diagram II shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/f0/f00f882c97fd201178e54f29151a48a4f41d4108cf375104cc338e968c55761b.png)\n\n- Diagram III shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/6e/6e0c0320775d93364e32655d1e09081382078fa7e96fbe621a8c558f63dfcabb.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111171 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110587 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b834b64-9679-56c2-b5e9-ee26a54b5e13" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Values in the Domain of the Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3d0ffb3-c274-5957-9de8-6b860acbbd7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108752} {:answer/id #uuid "a859f75b-ba7d-567a-a4b7-320edbe56d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108753} {:answer/id #uuid "06641cb4-3269-5b14-99e4-274d3d80801d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108754} {:answer/id #uuid "1801a405-2674-52af-b898-ee70bf4a6b0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108755} {:answer/id #uuid "438502c3-9194-55c3-9